{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":208863,"duration_api_ms":207942,"num_turns":33,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"23b44c2d-6ad7-474d-b2a1-6c19df43f82b","total_cost_usd":1.0596732500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":27,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45971,"cache_read_input_tokens":1126439,"output_tokens":8360,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":27,"outputTokens":8360,"cacheReadInputTokens":1126439,"cacheCreationInputTokens":45971,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0596732500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `emit_molt_failure` (shrimp.rs ~line 1380-1381), the `critical_gh_failure` computation lacks the `params.gh_min_d > 0.0` guard that was added to `critical_gh_deficit` in `molt_cycle` (line 554-555). When `gh_min_d == 0.0` (user disables GH minimum), the event path computes `gh_ratio = 0/0.01 = 0` which falsely triggers `critical_gh_failure`, emitting a misleading \"critical GH ratio 0.00<0.30\" detail instead of the correct \"score X<Y\" form. Fix: add the same `params.gh_min_d > 0.0 &&` guard to line 1381, i.e. `let critical_gh_failure = params.gh_min_d > 0.0 && gh_ratio < params.critical_molt_gh_ratio;`","rationale":"Diagnostic consistency bug. The event reporting path disagrees with the molt resolution path about whether a critical GH deficit occurred. This violates the acceptance criterion that events 'expose enough detail to explain why molt failure occurred' — it would explain a failure with a cause the simulation didn't actually use. The test `test_zero_ca_and_mg_min_parameters_use_defensive_guards` doesn't catch this because it asserts `last_molt_success == true` (the molt succeeds, so `emit_molt_failure` is never called). A test where `gh_min_d=0`, minerals are absent, and condition is poor enough to fail the molt would surface the misleading event."}],"summary":"Reviewed the 5-file diff introducing `temp_condition_min_factor` as a named parameter (replacing hardcoded 0.25), and adding a `gh_min_d > 0.0` guard to the `critical_gh_deficit` check in `molt_cycle`. The temp-factor refactor is clean: the old hardcoded floor is replaced with the species parameter everywhere (implementation, tests in events.rs and molt_mineral_budget.rs), validation accepts 0.0, and a defensive `.max(0.01)` epsilon prevents division-by-zero. The new test `test_temp_condition_min_factor_controls_molt_cadence_floor` correctly demonstrates that lowering the floor delays molt readiness under cold conditions. The zero-GH-minimum test correctly verifies that disabling mineral minimums doesn't trip the critical-GH hard-fail path. One real bug found: the `emit_molt_failure` event-reporting function computes its own `critical_gh_failure` flag without the new `gh_min_d > 0.0` guard, creating a diagnostic inconsistency where events blame \"critical GH ratio\" when the simulation itself did not treat the GH deficit as critical."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"91a52a57-d21d-49fd-9008-9af630416a49"}
